6.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {LSO r. 3.3-3 (reasonable belief in imminent death/serious harm + disclosure necessary to prevent it) governs. Eric’s explicit statements (“bought gun last week,” “tonight,” “end things for both of us” at ex-wife’s apartment) meet imminence; police contact was only practical prevention means. 

Round-2 record: 21/21 colleagues now affirm E. Colleague 12 and Colleague 8 switched from C to E. Defenses uniformly stress real-time/good-faith calibration under commentary (“reasonably necessary” judged prospectively when police request identifiers/locations for mobile, same-evening search); Florida addresses and children’s identities tied to flight risk, household confirmation, and Eric’s own statements—not extraneous. 

Persistent tension resolved: scope of “necessary” is prospective, not post-hoc minimalism; C’s stricter hindsight filter rejected as chilling the exception. Key preserved evidence: exact threat wording, exact data list sent, rule text + commentary. No change to assessment favoring E.}

